## Return Types & Widget Rendering

Your return value determines how results are displayed in the widget:

| Return Type | Widget Rendered | Notes |
|-------------|-----------------|-------|
| `pandas.DataFrame` | AG Grid Table | Best for tabular data. Recommended. |
| `snowflake.snowpark.DataFrame` | AG Grid Table | Auto-converted to pandas |
| `list[Row]` (from `.collect()`) | JSON Viewer | Raw Snowpark rows as variant |
| `plotly.graph_objects.Figure` | Plotly Chart | Interactive chart |
| `altair.Chart` | Altair Chart | Declarative visualization |
| `str` | Text Display | Plain text output |
| `dict` or `list` | JSON Viewer | Displayed as formatted JSON |
| `int`, `float`, `bool` | Text Display | Scalar values as text |

**Recommendations:**
- For tabular data: Use `.to_pandas()` to get an AG Grid table
- For charts: Return the figure/chart object directly (`fig` or `chart`)
- Avoid returning raw `.collect()` results unless JSON format is specifically needed

